		{
			"id": "s3_t",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1272,
			"y": 410,
			"width": 132.2559356689453,
			"height": 20,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#15803d",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "ae",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 255674348,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 1621332436,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1778899739690,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "ELEVATED GGT",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "ELEVATED GGT",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "s3_b",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1272,
			"y": 438,
			"width": 465.36240856969187,
			"height": 307.0031915622177,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "af",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 67927252,
			"version": 215,
			"versionNonce": 932925992,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1778901068503,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Primary utility: Confirms ALP is hepatic in origin\n(GGT is NOT present in bone — critical distinction)\n\nSTEP 1: HF-specific interpretation\n- GGT + ALP + TBili = cholestatic triad of congestive hepatopathy\n- Correlates with JVD, edema, TR grade, NYHA class, right-sided filling pressures\n- GGT inversely associated with survival in stable HF patients\n\nSTEP 2: Non-cardiac causes to exclude\n- Alcohol: GGT elevated in >50% of heavy drinkers even without overt liver\ndisease (most sensitive marker of alcohol intake)\n- Medications: phenytoin, barbiturates, carbamazepine\n- Pancreatic disease, DM, renal failure\n- NAFLD / NASH\n- Biliary obstruction (same as ALP workup)\n\nSTEP 3: Management\n- GGT alone NOT a standalone screening test\n- In HF-ICU: elevated GGT -> assess right-sided hemodynamics -> decongestion\n\nNOTE: Low GGT is not a recognized clinical entity and does not require workup.",
			"fontSize": 11.695359678560674,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Primary utility: Confirms ALP is hepatic in origin\n(GGT is NOT present in bone — critical distinction)\n\nSTEP 1: HF-specific interpretation\n- GGT + ALP + TBili = cholestatic triad of congestive hepatopathy\n- Correlates with JVD, edema, TR grade, NYHA class, right-sided filling pressures\n- GGT inversely associated with survival in stable HF patients\n\nSTEP 2: Non-cardiac causes to exclude\n- Alcohol: GGT elevated in >50% of heavy drinkers even without overt liver disease (most sensitive marker of alcohol intake)\n- Medications: phenytoin, barbiturates, carbamazepine\n- Pancreatic disease, DM, renal failure\n- NAFLD / NASH\n- Biliary obstruction (same as ALP workup)\n\nSTEP 3: Management\n- GGT alone NOT a standalone screening test\n- In HF-ICU: elevated GGT -> assess right-sided hemodynamics -> decongestion\n\nNOTE: Low GGT is not a recognized clinical entity and does not require workup.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": "Primary utility: Confirms ALP is hepatic in origin\n(GGT is NOT present in bone — critical distinction)\n\nSTEP 1: HF-specific interpretation\n- GGT + ALP + TBili = cholestatic triad of congestive hepatopathy\n- Correlates with JVD, edema, TR grade, NYHA class, right-sided filling pressures\n- GGT inversely associated with survival in stable HF patients\n\nSTEP 2: Non-cardiac causes to exclude\n- Alcohol: GGT elevated in >50% of heavy drinkers even without overt liver disease (most sensitive marker of alcohol intake)\n- Medications: phenytoin, barbiturates, carbamazepine\n- Pancreatic disease, DM, renal failure\n- NAFLD / NASH\n- Biliary obstruction (same as ALP workup)\n\nSTEP 3: Management\n- GGT alone NOT a standalone screening test\n- In HF-ICU: elevated GGT -> assess right-sided hemodynamics -> decongestion\n\nNOTE: Low GGT is not a recognized clinical entity and does not require workup."
		},
