			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1778899783996,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "No -> 3 most common ICU causes:",
			"fontSize": 14,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "No -> 3 most common ICU causes:",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "s7_no_b",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1520,
			"y": 1422,
			"width": 201.1556396484375,
			"height": 405,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b0V",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 404872812,
			"version": 3,
			"versionNonce": 676484820,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1778899783996,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "1. Vit K deficiency (39.6%)\n   Low FVII, FX, Prot C, Prot S\n   -> Poor nutrition, antibiotics,\n   biliary obstruction\n   -> Rx: Vitamin K IV or PO;\n   plasma generally avoidable\n\n2. Liver disease pattern (35.4%)\n   Low FV, low/normal fibrinogen,\n   high FVIII\n   -> Impaired hepatic synthesis\n   -> In HF: correlates with TBili,\n   GGT, IVC, TR severity\n   -> Plasma NOT for routine INR\n   correction in liver disease\n\n3. Occult DOAC effect (14.6%)\n   Anti-Xa DOAC on assay despite\n   no reported anticoagulant use\n\nACLI: ~80-84% show >=50% drop\nin prothrombin activity\n(distinguishes from viral hepatitis)\n\nPersistent coagulopathy despite\nhemo optimization -> suggests\nprogression to cardiac cirrhosis",
			"fontSize": 12,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "1. Vit K deficiency (39.6%)\n   Low FVII, FX, Prot C, Prot S\n   -> Poor nutrition, antibiotics,\n   biliary obstruction\n   -> Rx: Vitamin K IV or PO;\n   plasma generally avoidable\n\n2. Liver disease pattern (35.4%)\n   Low FV, low/normal fibrinogen,\n   high FVIII\n   -> Impaired hepatic synthesis\n   -> In HF: correlates with TBili,\n   GGT, IVC, TR severity\n   -> Plasma NOT for routine INR\n   correction in liver disease\n\n3. Occult DOAC effect (14.6%)\n   Anti-Xa DOAC on assay despite\n   no reported anticoagulant use\n\nACLI: ~80-84% show >=50% drop\nin prothrombin activity\n(distinguishes from viral hepatitis)\n\nPersistent coagulopathy despite\nhemo optimization -> suggests\nprogression to cardiac cirrhosis",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
